Fire has long been one of the greatest existential threats to a building and its occupants. But fire escapes became widespread kind of late in the game. Back in the 1700s, fire escapes weren't built-in features, but rather mobile ladders on carts hauled to blazes by firemen. Other solutions for escaping a fire in a multi-story building in the 1800s included parachute hats. I think you can imagine both how those looked and how they did not work at all. There was even this widely circulated plan that proposed that if there was a fire that archers from the ground would shoot arrows with ropes attached to them for residents on the upper floors to shimmy down. But eventually, we settled on iron fire escapes attached permanently to a building's facade. Fire escapes are thankfully not used very often, but unfortunately this also means that they can fall into disrepair, especially if a landlord is prone to cutting corners.
长期以来，火灾一直是建筑物及其 occupants 面临的最大生存威胁之一。但防火梯在游戏后期才普及。早在18世纪，防火梯还不是内置设施，而是消防员拖到火灾现场的手推车上的移动梯子。19世纪多层建筑中逃生火灾的其他解决方案包括降落伞帽。我想你可以想象它们的样貌以及它们是如何完全不起作用的。甚至还有一个广泛流传的计划，提议如果发生火灾，地面的弓箭手会射出带有绳索的箭，让高楼层的居民顺着绳索滑下来。但最终，我们确定了永久固定在建筑外墙上的铁制防火梯。谢天谢地，防火梯不常使用，但不幸的是，这也意味着它们可能会失修，特别是如果房东喜欢偷工减料的话。

